{"repositoryId":1327230913,"availability":"available","full":"AnayGarodia/sketchling","name":"sketchling","description":"A hand-drawn illustration and animation language for LLMs","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":26,"forks":2,"created":"2026-08-07T22:56:19Z","updated":"2026-08-16T21:21:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["ai-agents","animation","claude-code","cli","creative-coding","generative-art","gsap","hand-drawn","illustration","llm","motion-graphics","roughjs","svg","typescript"],"demo":"https://anaygarodia.github.io/sketchling/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.331Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.331Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.331Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.331Z","stars":26,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A hand drawn illustration and animation language for LLMs. Manim gave language models a way to express math visually in code. Sketchling does the same for expressive, hand drawn illustration and motion — not a diagramming DSL, not a general 3D engine, a vocabulary for drawing and moving things by hand.","This is the closing shot of The Lantern Maker, a nine scene, three minute short film. An artisan crafts a paper lantern by lamplight, then carries it through a darkening town to release it from a bridge at night. Watch the full thing at docs/story-lantern-maker.mp4.","Nobody hand animated this. Devin built it cold, working from nothing but this repository's own docs, the same way every example in examples/ was built: an LLM writing TypeScript against a vocabulary, not a human hand authoring vector art. That is the actual point of sketchling. If a coding agent can read a README and come out the other side with a real hand drawn film, the vocabulary is doing its job."],"features":["The vocabulary is expressive, not geometric. There is no Circle() or Arc(). Primitives take character parameters like weight, looseness, and energy, not just coordinates. A loose stroke hides imprecision by design…","The renderer is forgiving by default. Every shape draws through a rough.js based sketchy engine: jittered strokes, imperfect closure, variable width. Slightly off geometry reads as style, not as a mistake, the same…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AnayGarodia/sketchling/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"91c6b18e8f93e8e8862040d431aee3f9f1e7f990ca05fe7792ac65fa46bf94a9","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.477Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.477Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A hand drawn illustration and animation language for LLMs. Manim gave language models a way to express math visually in code. Sketchling does the same for expressive, hand drawn illustration and motion — not a diagramming DSL, not a general 3D engine, a vocabulary for drawing and moving things by hand.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AnayGarodia/sketchling/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"91c6b18e8f93e8e8862040d431aee3f9f1e7f990ca05fe7792ac65fa46bf94a9","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AnayGarodia/sketchling/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.477Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-16T21:21:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AnayGarodia/sketchling/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:39.477Z","hash":"91c6b18e8f93e8e8862040d431aee3f9f1e7f990ca05fe7792ac65fa46bf94a9","originalBytes":11041,"storedBytes":11041,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["sketchling","docs","hand","one","same","every","scene","gallery","vocabulary","animation","built","drawn","install","instead","lantern","look","real","three","agents.md","full","how","just","marketing","render","scenes","texture","through","way","agent","agents","chromium","code","coding","cold","examples","five","illustration","ink","license","line","maker","npm","pixel","scene.ts","two","whole","actually"